{%- comment -%}
  Echoes `url` with its `page=1` query parameter removed, so page 1 is always linked as
  the bare URL instead of the duplicate "?page=1". Only pass URLs known to target page 1:
  on any other URL the `remove` filters would eat the start of "page=10".

  The `&amp;` forms come first: content_for_header HTML-escapes the ampersands in its
  href attributes, while paginate URLs carry a raw `&`.

  Usage: {% render 'alc-page-1-url', url: paginate.previous.url %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{{- url
  | replace: '?page=1&amp;', '?'
  | replace: '&amp;page=1&amp;', '&amp;'
  | remove: '&amp;page=1'
  | replace: '?page=1&', '?'
  | replace: '&page=1&', '&'
  | remove: '&page=1'
  | remove: '?page=1'
-}}
